{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"25":{"eng-name":"Chapters on Hajj Rituals","ara-name":"كتاب المناسك"}},"section_detail":{"25":{"hadithnumber_first":2882,"hadithnumber_last":3119,"arabicnumber_first":2882,"arabicnumber_last":3119}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2890,"arabicnumber":2890,"text":"Rapporté par Anas bin Malik : Le Prophète (ﷺ) a accompli le Hajj sur une vieille selle, portant un manteau qui valait quatre dirhams ou moins. Puis il a dit : “Ô Allah, un Hajj sans ostentation ni recherche de réputation.”","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":25,"hadith":9},"chapter":{"id":4,"ara-name":"باب الْحَجِّ عَلَى الرَّحْلِ","eng-name":"Hajj on a saddle","isFirstHadith":true}}]}